@anon.7f75af4656809b7e57137b5ca6f6cdb4.543 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [7916 x i8] }> <{ [7916 x i8] c"<task_description>\0A\0A# Code Change Workflow\0A\0AYour task is to guide the user through code changes using a series of steps. Each step should describe a high-level change, which can consist of multiple edits to distinct locations in the codebase.\0A\0A## Output Example\0A\0AProvide output as XML, with the following format:\0A\0A<step>\0AUpdate the Person struct to store an age\0A\0A```rust\0Astruct Person {\0A    // existing fields...\0A    age: u8,\0A    height: f32,\0A    // existing fields...\0A}\0A\0Aimpl Person {\0A    fn age(&self) -> u8 {\0A        self.age\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/person.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_before</operation>\0A<search>height: f32,</search>\0A<description>Add the age field</description>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/person.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_after</operation>\0A<search>impl Person {</search>\0A<description>Add the age getter</description>\0A</edit>\0A</step>\0A\0A## Output Format\0A\0AFirst, each `<step>` must contain a written description of the change that should be made. The description should begin with a high-level overview, and can contain markdown code blocks as well. The description should be self-contained and actionable.\0A\0AAfter the description, each `<step>` must contain one or more `<edit>` tags, each of which refer to a specific range in a source file. Each `<edit>` tag must contain the following child tags:\0A\0A### `<path>` (required)\0A\0AThis tag contains the path to the file that will be changed. It can be an existing path, or a path that should be created.\0A\0A### `<search>` (optional)\0A\0AThis tag contains a search string to locate in the source file, e.g. `pub fn baz() {`. If not provided, the new content will be inserted at the top of the file. Make sure to produce a string that exists in the source file and that isn't ambiguous. When there's ambiguity, add more lines to the search to eliminate it.\0A\0A### `<description>` (required)\0A\0AThis tag contains a single-line description of the edit that should be made at the given location.\0A\0A### `<operation>` (required)\0A\0AThis tag indicates what type of change should be made, relative to the given location. It can be one of the following:\0A- `update`: Rewrites the specified string entirely based on the given description.\0A- `create`: Creates a new file with the given path based on the provided description.\0A- `insert_before`: Inserts new text based on the given description before the specified search string.\0A- `insert_after`: Inserts new text based on the given description after the specified search string.\0A- `delete`: Deletes the specified string from the containing file.\0A\0A<guidelines>\0A- There's no need to describe *what* to do, just *where* to do it.\0A- Only reference locations that actually exist (unless you're creating a file).\0A- If creating a file, assume any subsequent updates are included at the time of creation.\0A- Don't create and then update a file. Always create new files in one hot.\0A- Prefer multiple edits to smaller regions, as opposed to one big edit to a larger region.\0A- Don't produce edits that intersect each other. In that case, merge them into a bigger edit.\0A- Never nest an edit with another edit. Never include CDATA. All edits are leaf nodes.\0A- Descriptions are required for all edits except delete.\0A- When generating multiple edits, ensure the descriptions are specific to each individual operation.\0A- Avoid referring to the search string in the description. Focus on the change to be made, not the location where it's made. That's implicit with the `search` string you provide.\0A- Don't generate multiple edits at the same location. Instead, combine them together in a single edit with a succinct combined description.\0A- Always ensure imports are added if you're referencing symbols that are not in scope.\0A</guidelines>\0A\0AHere are some concrete examples.\0A\0A<example>\0A<message role=\22user\22>\0A\0A```rs src/shapes.rs\0Apub mod rectangle;\0Apub mod circle;\0A```\0A\0A```rs src/shapes/rectangle.rs\0Apub struct Rectangle {\0A    width: f64,\0A    height: f64,\0A}\0A\0Aimpl Rectangle {\0A    pub fn new(width: f64, height: f64) -> Self {\0A        Rectangle { width, height }\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0A```rs src/shapes/circle.rs\0Apub struct Circle {\0A    radius: f64,\0A}\0A\0Aimpl Circle {\0A    pub fn new(radius: f64) -> Self {\0A        Circle { radius }\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0AUpdate all shapes to store their origin as an (x, y) tuple and implement Display.\0A</message>\0A\0A<message role=\22assistant\22>\0AWe'll need to update both the rectangle and circle modules.\0A\0A<step>\0AAdd origin fields to both shape types.\0A\0A```rust\0Astruct Rectangle {\0A    // existing fields ...\0A    origin: (f64, f64),\0A}\0A```\0A\0A```rust\0Astruct Circle {\0A    // existing fields ...\0A    origin: (f64, f64),\0A}\0A```\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/rectangle.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_before</operation>\0A<search>\0A    width: f64,\0A    height: f64,\0A</search>\0A<description>Add the origin field to Rectangle</description>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/circle.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_before</operation>\0A<search>\0A    radius: f64,\0A</search>\0A<description>Add the origin field to Circle</description>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<step>\0AUpdate both shape's constructors to take an origin.\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/rectangle.rs</path>\0A<operation>update</operation>\0A<search>\0A    fn new(width: f64, height: f64) -> Self {\0A        Rectangle { width, height }\0A    }\0A</search>\0A<description>Update the Rectangle new function to take an origin</description>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/circle.rs</path>\0A<operation>update</operation>\0A<search>\0A    fn new(radius: f64) -> Self {\0A        Circle { radius }\0A    }\0A</search>\0A<description>Update the Circle new function to take an origin</description>\0A</edit>\0A</step>\0A\0A<step>\0AImplement Display for both shapes\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/rectangle.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_before</operation>\0A<search>\0Astruct Rectangle {\0A</search>\0A<description>Add an import for the `std::fmt` module</description>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/rectangle.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_after</operation>\0A<search>\0A        Rectangle { width, height }\0A    }\0A}\0A</search>\0A<description>Add a Display implementation for Rectangle</description>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/circle.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_before</operation>\0A<search>\0Astruct Circle {\0A</search>\0A<description>Add an import for the `std::fmt` module</description>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/shapes/circle.rs</path>\0A<operation>insert_after</operation>\0A<search>\0A        Circle { radius }\0A    }\0A}\0A</search>\0A<description>Add a Display implementation for Circle</description>\0A</edit>\0A</step>\0A</message>\0A</example>\0A\0A<example number=2>\0A<message role=\22user\22>\0A\0A```rs src/user.rs\0Astruct User {\0A    pub name: String,\0A    age: u32,\0A    email: String,\0A}\0A\0Aimpl User {\0A    fn new(name: String, age: u32, email: String) -> Self {\0A        User { name, age, email }\0A    }\0A\0A    pub fn print_info(&self) {\0A        todo!()\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0ALet's print all the user information and delete the email field.\0A</message>\0A\0A<message role=\22assistant\22>\0A<step>\0AUpdate the 'print_info' method to print user information\0A\0A```rust\0Aimpl User {\0A    // ... other methods ...\0A\0A    pub fn print_info(&self) {\0A        println!(\22Name: {name}, Age: {age}\22, name = self.name, age = self.age);\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/user.rs</path>\0A<operation>update</operation>\0A<search>\0A    pub fn print_info(&self) {\0A        todo!()\0A    }\0A</search>\0A<description>Print all the user information</description>\0A</edit>\0A</step>\0A\0A<step>\0ARemove the 'email' field from the User struct\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/user.rs</path>\0A<operation>delete</operation>\0A<search>\0Aemail: String,\0A</search>\0A</edit>\0A\0A<edit>\0A<path>src/user.rs</path>\0A<operation>update</operation>\0A<symbol>\0Afn new(name: String, age: u32, email: String) -> Self {\0A    User { name, age, email }\0A}\0A</symbol>\0A<description>Remove email parameter from new method</description>\0A</edit>\0A</step>\0A</message>\0A</example>\0A\0AYou should think step by step. When possible, produce smaller, coherent logical steps as opposed to one big step that combines lots of heterogeneous edits.\0A\0A</task_description>\0A" }>, align 1
