@anon.7f75af4656809b7e57137b5ca6f6cdb4.547 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [11485 x i8] }> <{ [11485 x i8] c"<overview>\0AYour task is to map a step from a workflow to locations in source code where code needs to be changed to fulfill that step.\0AGiven a workflow containing background context plus a series of <step> tags, you will resolve *one* of these step tags to resolve to one or more locations in the code.\0AWith each location, you will produce a brief, one-line description of the changes to be made.\0A\0A<guidelines>\0A- There's no need to describe *what* to do, just *where* to do it.\0A- Only reference locations that actually exist (unless you're creating a file).\0A- If creating a file, assume any subsequent updates are included at the time of creation.\0A- Don't create and then update a file. Always create new files in shot.\0A- Prefer updating symbols lower in the syntax tree if possible.\0A- Never include suggestions on a parent symbol and one of its children in the same suggestions block.\0A- Never nest an operation with another operation or include CDATA or other content. All suggestions are leaf nodes.\0A- Descriptions are required for all suggestions except delete.\0A- When generating multiple suggestions, ensure the descriptions are specific to each individual operation.\0A- Avoid referring to the location in the description. Focus on the change to be made, not the location where it's made. That's implicit with the symbol you provide.\0A- Don't generate multiple suggestions at the same location. Instead, combine them together in a single operation with a succinct combined description.\0A- To add imports respond with a suggestion where the `\22symbol\22` key is set to `\22#imports\22`\0A</guidelines>\0A</overview>\0A\0A<examples>\0A<example>\0A<workflow_context>\0A<message role=\22user\22>\0A```rs src/rectangle.rs\0Astruct Rectangle {\0A    width: f64,\0A    height: f64,\0A}\0A\0Aimpl Rectangle {\0A    fn new(width: f64, height: f64) -> Self {\0A        Rectangle { width, height }\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A\0AWe need to add methods to calculate the area and perimeter of the rectangle. Can you help with that?\0A</message>\0A<message role=\22assistant\22>\0ASure, I can help with that!\0A\0A<step>Add new methods 'calculate_area' and 'calculate_perimeter' to the Rectangle struct</step>\0A<step>Implement the 'Display' trait for the Rectangle struct</step>\0A</message>\0A</workflow_context>\0A\0A<step_to_resolve>\0AAdd new methods 'calculate_area' and 'calculate_perimeter' to the Rectangle struct\0A</step_to_resolve>\0A\0A<incorrect_output reason=\22NEVER append multiple children at the same location.\22>\0A{\0A  \22title\22: \22Add Rectangle methods\22,\0A  \22suggestions\22: [\0A    {\0A      \22kind\22: \22AppendChild\22,\0A      \22path\22: \22src/shapes.rs\22,\0A      \22symbol\22: \22impl Rectangle\22,\0A      \22description\22: \22Add calculate_area method\22\0A    },\0A    {\0A      \22kind\22: \22AppendChild\22,\0A      \22path\22: \22src/shapes.rs\22,\0A      \22symbol\22: \22impl Rectangle\22,\0A      \22description\22: \22Add calculate_perimeter method\22\0A    }\0A  ]\0A}\0A</incorrect_output>\0A\0A<correct_output>\0A{\0A  \22title\22: \22Add Rectangle methods\22,\0A  \22suggestions\22: [\0A    {\0A      \22kind\22: \22AppendChild\22,\0A      \22path\22: \22src/shapes.rs\22,\0A      \22symbol\22: \22impl Rectangle\22,\0A      \22description\22: \22Add calculate area and perimeter methods\22\0A    }\0A  ]\0A}\0A</correct_output>\0A\0A<step_to_resolve>\0AImplement the 'Display' trait for the Rectangle struct\0A</step_to_resolve>\0A\0A<output>\0A{\0A  \22title\22: \22Implement Display for Rectangle\22,\0A  \22suggestions\22: [\0A    {\0A      \22kind\22: \22InsertSiblingAfter\22,\0A      \22path\22: \22src/shapes.rs\22,\0A      \22symbol\22: \22impl Rectangle\22,\0A      \22description\22: \22Implement Display trait for Rectangle\22\0A    }\0A  ]\0A}\0A</output>\0A\0A<example>\0A<workflow_context>\0A<message role=\22user\22>\0A```rs src/user.rs\0Astruct User {\0A    pub name: String,\0A    age: u32,\0A    email: String,\0A}\0A\0Aimpl User {\0A    fn new(name: String, age: u32, email: String) -> Self {\0A        User { name, age, email }\0A    }\0A\0A    pub fn print_info(&self) {\0A        println!(\22Name: {}, Age: {}, Email: {}\22, self.name, self.age, self.email);\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A</message>\0A<message role=\22assistant\22>\0ACertainly!\0A<step>Update the 'print_info' method to use formatted output</step>\0A<step>Remove the 'email' field from the User struct</step>\0A</message>\0A</workflow_context>\0A\0A<step_to_resolve>\0AUpdate the 'print_info' method to use formatted output\0A</step_to_resolve>\0A\0A<output>\0A{\0A  \22title\22: \22Use formatted output\22,\0A  \22suggestions\22: [\0A    {\0A      \22kind\22: \22Update\22,\0A      \22path\22: \22src/user.rs\22,\0A      \22symbol\22: \22impl User pub fn print_info\22,\0A      \22description\22: \22Use formatted output\22\0A    }\0A  ]\0A}\0A</output>\0A\0A<step_to_resolve>\0ARemove the 'email' field from the User struct\0A</step_to_resolve>\0A\0A<output>\0A{\0A  \22title\22: \22Remove email field\22,\0A  \22suggestions\22: [\0A      {\0A        \22kind\22: \22Delete\22,\0A        \22path\22: \22src/user.rs\22,\0A        \22symbol\22: \22struct User email\22\0A      }\0A    ]\0A}\0A</output>\0A</example>\0A\0A<example>\0A<workflow_context>\0A<message role=\22user\22>\0A```rs src/vehicle.rs\0Astruct Vehicle {\0A    make: String,\0A    model: String,\0A    year: u32,\0A}\0A\0Aimpl Vehicle {\0A    fn new(make: String, model: String, year: u32) -> Self {\0A        Vehicle { make, model, year }\0A    }\0A\0A    fn print_year(&self) {\0A        println!(\22Year: {}\22, self.year);\0A    }\0A}\0A```\0A</message>\0A<message role=\22assistant\22>\0A<step>Add a 'use std::fmt;' statement at the beginning of the file</step>\0A<step>Add a new method 'start_engine' in the Vehicle impl block</step>\0A</message>\0A</workflow_cont